sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-willistoni-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-willistoni-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-willistoni-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila willistoni subcellular Turing wavelength (1.5 µm, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 86.9/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2. The same Schnakenberg reconstruction is now fingerprinted. A six-point diffusivity sweep matches the analytical wavelength with Pearson r = 1 and RMSE at roundoff on commensurate modes. The noise-seeded field selects 1.480 µm against the 1.466 µm reference. Equal diffusivities drive the seeded stripe to a flat field. The Hanson abdomen is segmented; coherency, foreground fraction, and KS are recorded with values that are not copies of the references. Scale 1.5 µm, age 0 Ma. Virilis (predecessor) 1.676 µm and 7.40 granules per cell; willistoni 1.466 µm and 5.77; yakuba (successor) 1.509 µm and 6.09. Overall 86.9/100 (faithfulness 86.3, reproducibility 88.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_willistoni_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-willistoni-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/gif, 1833875 B, 720×540 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 481ccd337d573ff3027fbb3cc9c1b91d39c61e61a01ed5031ce0d44d23ba727f (sha256 481ccd337d573ff3027fbb3cc9c1b91d39c61e61a01ed5031ce0d44d23ba727f), spec_fingerprint db43d14901fb6b4601bb2d4fcd69a0bd3c5388cab0d6eb64de70aadd7ba01054. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: db43d14901fb6b4601bb2d4fcd69a0bd3c5388cab0d6eb64de70aadd7ba01054; artifact_sha256: 481ccd337d573ff3027fbb3cc9c1b91d39c61e61a01ed5031ce0d44d23ba727f. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-willistoni-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 gives the diffusion-driven instability and the critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979 gives the two-species kinetics used here. | Clark et al. 2007 describe the D. willistoni genome, sex-comb loss, and inversion polymorphism. | Jeong et al. 2008 and Wittkopp et al. 2009 describe Drosophila abdominal pigmentation divergence relevant to the yakuba successor and the virilis-group predecessor. | Hanson 2019 is a CC BY-SA 4.0 photograph of an adult D. willistoni female.; reconstructed_in_script: a=0.072, b=1.186, gamma=0.84, Du=0.015919 µm², Dv=0.214909 µm² are chosen so λ_max=1.466 µm. | Allometry λ ∝ L_body^0.35 and a cell diameter linear in body length are slot-specific reconstructions. | The periodic patch stands in for the repeating granule lattice inside an epidermal cell.; transfer_boundary: The photograph resolves the whole fly. The 1.5 µm field is painted onto the segmented abdomen; it is not a micrograph of granules.; does_not_claim: Does not claim Clark 2007 measured a 1.5 µm Turing wavelength. | Does not claim sex-comb loss is produced by this reaction-diffusion system. | Does not claim D. virilis is a literal ancestor or D. yakuba a literal descendant. | Does not reuse slot 2931 parameters (86 µm, alpha_scale 1.63, beta_offset 0.38).." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.869"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7, loop 3211 primary assessor, pass 2" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

